{
  "id": "kk3t52s7n1VDRL2N",
  "name": "Curate n8n GitHub Releases into Blog Drafts with a Claude Relevance Check",
  "tags": [],
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "sticky-overview",
      "name": "Overview & Setup",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -2128,
        -1008
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 780,
        "height": 832,
        "content": "## Curate n8n GitHub Releases into Blog Drafts (Claude-judged)\n\n### How it works\n1. Runs every morning and fetches the latest n8n GitHub releases\n2. Skips releases already processed, keeps the 3 newest\n3. Asks Claude whether each one is genuinely newsworthy (new features only)\n4. If yes, Claude writes a first-person blog post (no speculation, no fabricated hands-on experience) and saves it as a WordPress draft\n5. If no, logs it as skipped so it's never re-checked\n6. Sends a LINE notification with a direct edit link to the new draft\n\n### Setup steps\n- [ ] Add an Anthropic API key credential (Header Auth) on both Claude nodes\n- [ ] Add a GitHub credential, and point the URL at your own repo if different\n- [ ] Add a Google Sheets credential (two tracking sheets: processed / skipped)\n- [ ] Add a WordPress credential\n- [ ] (Optional) Add a LINE Messaging API credential (Header Auth) \u2014 or just delete the LINE node\n- [ ] Open the \"Config (edit me)\" node and fill in your blog name, persona, URL and WordPress category ID\n\n### Customization\nThe relevance-check and writing prompts (in the two Claude nodes) can be freely rewritten for a different tone, language or source repo."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
